{title: There Is a Redeemer (FJ_196_en)}
{song_number: 196}
{language: en}
{tempo: 92}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D]There is a Redeemer, [G]Jesus, [D]God's own [A]Son,
[D]precious Lamb of [G]God, Mes[D]siah, [Em7]Ho[A7]ly [D]One.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D]Jesus my Redeemer, [G]name a[D]bove all [A]names,
[D]precious Lamb of [G]God, Mes[D]siah, [Em7]O for [A7]sinners [D]slain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Thank You, O my [G]Father, [D]for [Em]giving [A]us Your [D]Son,
[A]and [D]leaving Your [G]Spirit [D]till the [Em7]work on [A7]earth is [D]done.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D]When I stand in glory I will see His face.
And there I'll serve my King forever, in that holy place.
{end_of_verse}
